            <div xml:id="d592">

                <pb facs="0879" n="789" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg789"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/444: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia (Mitchell) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-24T16:00:00-00:44">December 24, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>115. Your telegram No. 78, December 23, noon, and 79, December 23, 3 p.m. Letter
                    delivered to Barclay at 11:30. British, French and German colleagues made
                    acquainted with the position of my Government. French and German in accord with
                    position taken. British undoubtedly sympathetic with Liberia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mitchell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
